 130: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
 131:     """
 132:     Move aligned singleton markers along straight sightlines until they touch the nearest 2x2 block, leaving non-sightline and lower-left distractor markers fixed.
 133: 
 134:     Input structure
 135:     - The background is the dominant color.
 136:     - One foreground color forms filled 2x2 blocks.
 137:     - The other foreground color forms singleton marker pixels.
 138: 
 139:     Rule
 140:     - For each marker, find clear horizontal or vertical sightlines to any 2x2 block and choose the unique nearest block by travel distance.
 141:     - Move that marker to the adjacent ring cell on the same row or column of the chosen block.
 142:     - Markers with no clear sightline stay in place; a lower-row marker to the left of a block also stays fixed when that block already has chosen vertical markers both above and below it.
 143: 
 144:     Key insight
 145:     - The red 2x2 blocks act as magnets, so each direct marker ray is compressed to the one-cell ring around its nearest block while unrelated singleton markers remain noise.
 146:     """
 147:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
 148:     assert g.ndim == 2, "expected a 2D grid"
